  "body": "What happens: `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` (crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs) fails on a platform that is not one of the three pinned triples. The `else` band still expects the pre-solidcore counts (4706..=4736 moves, 4678..=4708 planar feeds, 539..=559 arcs). A solidcore build gives about (3158, 3130, 1141), the same triple the pinned platforms expect.\n\nEvidence: the body of PR #3059 reports the step red at \"expected (4716, 4688, 549), produced (3158, 3130, 1141)\" on the author's machine, which is not Windows x86_64, Linux x86_64 or macOS arm64. The same failure reproduces on plain main: the PR does not touch the bore test or the planner.\n\nExpected: the band matches the solidcore counts, so the test passes on an unpinned platform until someone measures and adds its exact triple.\n\nDone means: the fallback band expects the solidcore triple (with a small band), and the test passes in release on a fourth platform or the band is shown green by the unit test that checks it.\n",
